{"parentUuid":"0d229991-0b24-4a50-a97f-4f5b16187874","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bs56uJt4a56ycpFHpnAZWa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"rectpack python library 2D rectangle packing 2026 status maintenance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - secnot/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"rectpack · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rectpack/\"},{\"title\":\"rectangle-packer\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rectangle-packer/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tobami/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tobami/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - javier-martinez-palmer/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/javier-martinez-palmer/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Sammbale7/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Sammbale7/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"secnot/rectpack\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack/issues\"},{\"title\":\"Rectangle Packaging Problem / Efficient 2D Packing | Maskset\",\"url\":\"https://www.maskset.net/blog/2023/10/19/rectangle-packaging-problem-/-efficient-2d-packing/\"},{\"title\":\"rpack — rectangle-packer 2.0.5 documentation - Read the Docs\",\"url\":\"https://rectangle-packer.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_modules/rpack.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - findux/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/findux/rectpack\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about the rectpack Python library:\n\n## Overview\n\nRectpack is a collection of heuristic algorithms for solving the 2D knapsack problem, also known as the bin packing problem. In essence packing a set of rectangles into the smallest number of bins.\n\n## Algorithm Implementation\n\nThe library implements three of the algorithms: Skyline, Maxrects, and Guillotine, with various variants.\n\n## Status and Maintenance\n\nThe search results show that rectpack is maintained on GitHub at the primary repository (github.com/secnot/rectpack), with documentation available on PyPI. There are also several forks available from other contributors. However, the search results don't contain specific information about the current maintenance status as of 2026 or recent activity details.\n\n## Features\n\nRectpack is thoroughly tested. The library supports various packing bin modes and sorting algorithms to optimize rectangle placement.\n\nFor the most current maintenance status and recent updates, I'd recommend checking the official GitHub repository directly (github.com/secnot/rectpack) to view recent commits, issues, and pull requests.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e93b4e62-2d51-4c3f-b7ff-d056211d72fe","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:34.232Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0d229991-0b24-4a50-a97f-4f5b16187874","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a5f4f021-ecae-48b6-88d5-5dfcb5586e92","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LVn6EqsipagVmu6DQkmUxi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"BinPacking2D ktnr python solver 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"BinPacking2D/packingSolver at master · ktnr/BinPacking2D\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D/tree/master/packingSolver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SebastianBitsch/bin-packing: Python solver for the 2D bin packing problem · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SebastianBitsch/bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack: A 2D bin/strip-packing problem solving python package\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack\"},{\"title\":\"Build software better, together\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/2d-bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"2D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/gMgPBryj1wA\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - mses-bly/2D-Bin-Packing: Library to solve 2D bin packing problems with irregular pieces. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mses-bly/2D-Bin-Packing\"},{\"title\":\"binpacking · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/binpacking/\"},{\"title\":\"Python and the Bin Packing Problem | Reintech media\",\"url\":\"https://reintech.io/blog/python-bin-packing-problem-guide\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about BinPacking2D ktnr Python solver:\n\nBinPacking2D is a Python solver that uses branch-and-cut for exact solutions to two-dimensional bin packing problems. The project provides exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut.\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n- The output indicates whether the solution is optimal and if the solution was found during the constructive phase by constraint programming (using Google's CP-SAT solver) or by branch-and-cut\n- The 2D-OPP (Optimal Placement Problem) subproblem is solved via CP, with or-tools implementing most of the described propagations\n- Available placement point patterns include unit discretization, normal patterns, and meet-in-the-middle\n\n**Performance:**\n\nThe algorithm produces optimal solutions for the majority of the 500 benchmark instances in less than 20 minutes. However, it has difficulty in proving feasibility/infeasibility of 2D-OPP subproblems for instances with many small items, with Google's CP-SAT solver sometimes taking more than 300 seconds.\n\nThe project is hosted on GitHub at ktnr/BinPacking2D and provides various parametrizable algorithmic features for customizing the solver behavior.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ccc49bf2-3d57-4c48-94af-67dec56ad958","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:36.185Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a5f4f021-ecae-48b6-88d5-5dfcb5586e92","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"bfb604ec-fcb7-4c32-8e7f-0977f7a4411f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018tjYXJRgiGSVKf6v6WYEHU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"py3dbp py2dbp python bin packing library\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"py3dbp · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/py3dbp/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - enzoruiz/3dbinpacking: A python library for 3D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/enzoruiz/3dbinpacking\"},{\"title\":\"Bin-Packing Add-on — ezdxf 1.4.3 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ezdxf.readthedocs.io/en/stable/addons/binpacking.html\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing Space: How Python Revolutionizes Packing Furniture for Storage and Moving | by Devin Richard Smith | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@devin.richard.smith/optimizing-space-how-python-revolutionizes-packing-furniture-for-storage-and-moving-b586d7b494d2\"},{\"title\":\"[Baseline] 3D-bin packing with py3dbp\",\"url\":\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/howeverforever/baseline-3d-bin-packing-with-py3dbp\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - jerry800416/3D-bin-packing: 3D Bin Packing improvements based on https://github.com/enzoruiz/3dbinpacking · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jerry800416/3D-bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"3D-bin-packing/example2.py at master · jerry800416/3D-bin-packing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/jerry800416/3D-bin-packing/blob/master/example2.py\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - totuk2/packer: based on 3dbinpack\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/totuk2/packer\"},{\"title\":\"py3dbp - Python Package Health Analysis | Snyk\",\"url\":\"https://snyk.io/advisor/python/py3dbp\"},{\"title\":\"Bin-Packing Add-on — ezdxf 1.4.0b1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://ezdxf.mozman.at/docs/addons/binpacking.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the py3dbp and py2dbp Python bin packing libraries:\n\n## Overview\n\npy3dbp, short for Python 3D Bin Packing, is a library designed to figure out the best way to fit items into a space without wasting material.\n\n## Key Features\n\nBy default, all bins and items are sorted from smallest to biggest, but this can be reversed to change the packing order. The library offers two main distribution modes:\n\n- With distribute_items=True, items are placed in bins such that at least one item fits in each bin, distributing all items across bins\n- With distribute_items=False, the algorithm attempts to fit all items in each bin and shows per bin which items were fitted and which were not\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nThe library provides three main classes:\n- `Packer()` - the packing algorithm\n- `Bin()` - represents a container with dimensions and max weight\n- `Item()` - represents items to be packed with dimensions and weight\n\n## Project Status\n\nThe maintenance status of py3dbp is Inactive, as it hasn't seen any new versions released to PyPI in the past 12 months. However, the package receives approximately 4,301 weekly downloads.\n\nThe search results primarily reference py3dbp; py2dbp appears to be a predecessor version for Python 2, though the search results focus mainly on the Python 3 version.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c3fcec74-aa6e-4b72-b8fd-403a423af59f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:37.653Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bfb604ec-fcb7-4c32-8e7f-0977f7a4411f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7e14ec87-21e2-41b5-9d3c-e9a6d0008616","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EYnoEaHuvYa8h9Mxk6RKMZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D strip packing solver python open source 2025 heuristic\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack: A 2D bin/strip-packing problem solving python package\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - seanys/2D-Irregular-Packing-Algorithm: Realize 2D irregular packing algorithm with python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/seanys/2D-Irregular-Packing-Algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - secnot/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"hyperpack · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/hyperpack/\"},{\"title\":\"An open-source heuristic to reboot 2D nesting research\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.13329v2\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - JeroenGar/sparrow: State-of-the-art nesting for 2D irregular strip packing · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow\"},{\"title\":\"packing-algorithm · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/packing-algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Extra material: Strip packing — Hands-On Mathematical Optimization with AMPL in Python\",\"url\":\"https://ampl.com/mo-book/notebooks/03/strip-packing.html\"},{\"title\":\"[2509.13329] An open-source heuristic to reboot 2D nesting research\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.13329\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - HolyChen/Strip-Packing: An algorithm for solving 2D strip packing problem. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/HolyChen/Strip-Packing\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key 2D strip packing solvers for Python with open-source heuristic approaches:\n\n## Notable Open-Source Solutions\n\n### Hyperpack\nHyperpack is the first open-source 2D-Binpacking problem solver and optimizer in Python, based on personally developed heuristics. The hyperpack library is an API for solving instances of the 2D Binpacking problem and also - as of v1.1.0 - strip packing instances, and is multiprocessing enabled to minimize execution times while utilizing only pure python, making the package dependency free.\n\n### Sparrow (2025)\nA heuristic for the 2D irregular strip packing problem that redefines both the academic and open-source state of the art, with implementation sparrow publicly available at: https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow. The core idea of the algorithm is to decompose the 2DISPP into a sequence of feasibility problems where the strip is converted into a container with fixed dimensions and items are temporarily allowed to collide, with a local-search algorithm iteratively moving colliding items to gradually resolve them.\n\n### Rectpack\nRectpack is a collection of heuristic algorithms for solving the 2D knapsack problem, also known as the bin packing problem, essentially packing a set of rectangles into the smallest number of bins.\n\n### 2D Irregular Packing Algorithm\nAnother open-source implementation is available at GitHub with implementations including approaches like solving irregular strip packing problems by hybridizing simulated annealing and linear programming.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6d69cb6e-31fb-46db-b34c-7adbd3313135","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:37.921Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7e14ec87-21e2-41b5-9d3c-e9a6d0008616","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
