{"parentUuid":"02b1cdd4-e3ae-4ed3-b3aa-8450bc102bdd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014j3LKa4Vr9ZuAPo6mCCj6G","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"sparrow JeroenGar 2D irregular strip packing 2025 rust\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - JeroenGar/sparrow: State-of-the-art nesting for 2D irregular strip packing · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow\"},{\"title\":\"sparrow/data/experiments/README.md at main · JeroenGar/sparrow\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow/blob/main/data/experiments/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"JeroenGar (Jeroen Gardeyn) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar\"},{\"title\":\"An open-source heuristic to reboot 2D nesting research\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.13329v1\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - PaulDL-RS/spyrrow: Python wrapper of Sparrow, State-of-the-art Nesting for 2D irregular strip packing\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/PaulDL-RS/spyrrow\"},{\"title\":\"Issues · JeroenGar/sparrow\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow/issues\"},{\"title\":\"sparrow/LICENSE at main · JeroenGar/sparrow\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/sparrow/blob/main/LICENSE\"},{\"title\":\"strip-packing · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/strip-packing?l=rust\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) An open-source heuristic to reboot 2D nesting research\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/395583530_An_open-source_heuristic_to_reboot_2D_nesting_research\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - JeroenGar/jagua-rs: A fast and fearless Collision Detection Engine for 2D nesting problems · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/JeroenGar/jagua-rs\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Sparrow, JeroenGar's 2D irregular strip packing solution in Rust:\n\n## Overview\n\nSparrow can be used to solve 2D irregular strip packing problems, also commonly referred to as nesting problems, and builds on jagua-rs: a collision detection engine for 2D irregular cutting & packing problems.\n\n## The Paper and Release\n\nThe paper introduced a heuristic for the 2D irregular strip packing problem (2DISPP) that redefines both the academic and open-source state of the art, with the implementation sparrow publicly available at GitHub. Sparrow is an open-source heuristic approach to solving 2D irregular strip packing problems that decomposes the optimization problem into a sequence of feasibility problems, where collisions between items are gradually resolved, and consistently outperforms the state of the art.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe implementation of the 2D nesting algorithm is written in Rust and called sparrow, publicly available at GitHub.\n\n## Real-World Applications\n\nSuch optimization problems arise in a wide range of industries such as garment manufacturing, furniture production, shipbuilding, printing, laser-cutting, metalworking, woodworking, foam-cutting, leather crafting, and microchip design.\n\nThe project represents a significant contribution to the field with the goal of making 2D nesting research more accessible through open-source tools and reproducible research practices.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1e3925ee-7bc6-4879-9821-2bc2a37409d7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:48.503Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"02b1cdd4-e3ae-4ed3-b3aa-8450bc102bdd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cbec009f-3fbc-428d-93ea-a964717658cb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M2KY65eULGtkZ92rBHHLYP","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"2D packing fixed mandatory placements warm start CP-SAT initial solution\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"A new search procedure for the two-dimensional orthogonal ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.dil.univ-mrs.fr/~gcolas/packing/jmma-20022015.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"2D bin packing on a grid - Stack Overflow\",\"url\":\"https://kiwix.ounapuu.ee/content/stackoverflow.com_en_all_2023-11/questions/47918792/2d-bin-packing-on-a-grid\"},{\"title\":\"2D Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/gMgPBryj1wA\"},{\"title\":\"A Simple Solution for Shape Packing in 2D\",\"url\":\"https://www.gorillasun.de/blog/a-simple-solution-for-shape-packing-in-2d/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information relevant to your query about 2D packing with CP-SAT:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**CP-SAT Constraint for 2D Packing:**\nThe add_no_overlap_2d constraint is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on two dimensions, e.g., for packing rectangles.\n\n**Warm Start and Initial Solutions:**\nFirst solution subsolvers are strategies that try to find a first solution as fast as possible and are often used to warm up the solver and to get a first impression of the problem.\n\n**Fixed/Mandatory Placements:**\nThe search results indicate that OR-Tools has a construct Constraint.OnlyEnforceIf(boolean) which can be used to conditionally enforce constraints, though the specific implementation for mandatory fixed placements isn't extensively covered in these results.\n\n**Initial Solutions from 2D-BPP:**\nStart solutions are generated by solving a 2D-BPP problem via CP.\n\nThe results show general CP-SAT techniques for 2D packing problems, but don't specifically detail how to implement warm start with fixed mandatory placements. For more detailed implementation guidance on these specific features combined together, you may want to consult the Google OR-Tools CP-SAT documentation directly or check for specialized tutorials on constraint programming warm starts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"321924a5-ad4d-42da-820b-c69426d36b20","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:50.269Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cbec009f-3fbc-428d-93ea-a964717658cb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0defea09-0769-48bd-8975-cc39a1436bc7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"eb903157-6eb9-4dd8-8710-2e428622c046","agentId":"add24b2dd9d00df6b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NWd7cYTGSoYjme4USFCJzy","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"hyperpack python 2D bin packing solver 2025 features\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack: A 2D bin/strip-packing problem solving python package\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/AlkiviadisAleiferis/hyperpack\"},{\"title\":\"hyperpack · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/hyperpack/\"},{\"title\":\"piwheels - hyperpack\",\"url\":\"https://www.piwheels.org/project/hyperpack/\"},{\"title\":\"bin-packing · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/bin-packing?l=python&o=desc&s=stars\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SebastianBitsch/bin-packing: Python solver for the 2D bin packing problem · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SebastianBitsch/bin-packing\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - secnot/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - ktnr/BinPacking2D: Exact solutions for two-dimensional bin packing problems by branch-and-cut · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ktnr/BinPacking2D\"},{\"title\":\"hyperpack · GitHub Topics · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/topics/hyperpack\"},{\"title\":\"binpacking · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/binpacking/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Flamethr0wer/polygon-packer: A powerful bin packing problem solver for any polygons · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Flamethr0wer/polygon-packer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about HyperPack, the Python 2D bin packing solver:\n\n## Overview\nHyperPack is the first open-source 2D-Binpacking problem solver and optimizer in Python, based on personally developed heuristics. The hyperpack library is an API for solving instances of the 2D Binpacking problem and also - as of v1.1.0 - strip packing instances.\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Performance & Design:**\n- The library is multiprocessing enabled to minimize execution times and utilizes only pure python, making the package dependency free.\n\n**Problem Capabilities:**\n- Any number and sizes of (rectangular) items, any number and sizes of (rectangular) bins (containers), and items can be rotated or not.\n\n**Solving Methods:**\nThe library supports multiple solving approaches including `hypersearch()` and `local_search()` methods for finding solutions.\n\n**Visualization:**\nPlotly (5.14.0 or greater) is needed for figure creation and kaleido (0.2.1 or greater) for figure exportation to image, though these libraries are not listed as dependencies providing liberty of figure implementation.\n\n**Current Version:**\nThe latest version available is 1.2.0.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about features added in 2025, as the codebase was last updated in November 2025 according to the GitHub topic page references.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5b1f49e2-9ab6-4b5d-9306-158b3d7ff42a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:06:50.607Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0defea09-0769-48bd-8975-cc39a1436bc7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
